<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "535 — 2026 midterms forecast" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff">
    <meta name="description" content="<%= content_for(:description) || "An agent-powered forecast of the 2026 U.S. Senate and House elections: correlated Monte Carlo simulation, live polling, transparent methodology." %>">
    <link rel="canonical" href="<%= content_for(:canonical_url) || canonical_url %>">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="application-name" content="535">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">

    <%= render "shared/fonts" %>

    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <%# Add to Home Screen. The manifest does not register a service worker:
        a cache would serve a stale forecast. %>
    <%= tag.link rel: "manifest", href: pwa_manifest_path(format: :json) %>

    <%# The SVG is the real mark and scales to any tab; the PNG is the fallback
        for browsers that don't take SVG favicons. apple-touch-icon is its own
        file rather than icon.png because iOS applies its own rounded mask —
        that variant is full-bleed with the art inset, so the mask has nothing
        to cut off. %>
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">

    <%# Includes all stylesheet files in app/assets/stylesheets %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>

    <%= render "shared/posthog" %>
  </head>

  <body class="min-h-screen bg-white text-slate-900 antialiased [font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums]<%= " max-xl:pb-[calc(3.75rem+env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]" if app_shell? %>">
    <a href="#main" class="sr-only focus-visible:not-sr-only focus-visible:absolute focus-visible:left-3 focus-visible:top-3 focus-visible:z-50 focus-visible:rounded focus-visible:bg-slate-900 focus-visible:px-3 focus-visible:py-2 focus-visible:text-white">
      Skip to content
    </a>

    <%# Below xl the public pages are an app shell: this thin top bar, and a
        fixed bottom bar after it. The eight-link nav is display:none there,
        so a phone without JavaScript reaches Polls, Pollsters, Methodology,
        About, and Privacy from #site-directory in the footer. More's href is
        that same anchor.

        The top bar is sticky. From lg to xl the chamber tables pin their
        column headers; application.css offsets those headers by this bar.

        From xl to just under 2xl the wordmark and the action cluster share
        the top row and the links take the full width underneath. One row
        waits until 2xl. Session, password, unsubscribe, and email-preferences
        pages are documents at every width: they keep the stacking header
        and do not get the bottom bar. %>
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]<%= " max-xl:sticky max-xl:top-0 max-xl:z-30" if app_shell? %>">
      <div class="<%= app_shell? ? "container mx-auto grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-0 px-5 py-2 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] xl:gap-x-8 xl:gap-y-1 2xl:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto]" : "container mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-1 px-5 py-2 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] 2xl:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto]" %>">
        <%# The stamp is beside the wordmark rather than inside the link: it
            dates the forecast, and a timestamp that navigates home when you
            click it is a small lie about what it is. %>
        <%# contents below xl so the stamp can take the full second line.
            At xl the group is a flex row again: wordmark, then the stamp. %>
        <div class="<%= app_shell? ? "contents xl:col-start-1 xl:row-start-1 xl:flex xl:min-w-0 xl:flex-none xl:flex-wrap xl:items-baseline xl:gap-x-2.5" : "col-start-1 row-start-1 flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2.5" %>">
          <%= link_to "535", root_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900#{ " col-start-1 row-start-1" if app_shell? }" %>
          <% if (run = latest_model_run) %>
            <span class="font-figure text-xs tracking-tight text-slate-600<%= " col-span-2 row-start-2 mt-0.5 xl:mt-0" if app_shell? %>" data-testid="header-updated">
              <%= Site::Format.last_updated(run.started_at) %>
            </span>
          <% end %>
        </div>

        <nav class="<%= app_shell? ? "hidden text-sm font-medium xl:col-start-1 xl:col-end-[-1] xl:row-start-2 xl:flex xl:min-w-0 xl:flex-wrap xl:items-center xl:gap-x-1 2xl:col-start-2 2xl:col-end-3 2xl:row-start-1" : "col-start-1 col-end-[-1] row-start-2 flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1 text-sm font-medium 2xl:col-start-2 2xl:col-end-3 2xl:row-start-1" %>" aria-label="Primary">
          <%# The groups stay in the markup so the reference links can take a
              small inset once they share a line with the forecast links.
              contents lets every link wrap in one row: a full-width group
              was leaving Dispatches, then About, alone on a narrow phone. %>
          <div class="contents">
            <%= nav_link "Dashboard", root_path %>
            <%= nav_link "Senate", senate_path %>
            <%= nav_link "House", house_path %>
            <%= nav_link "Dispatches", dispatches_path %>
          </div>
          <%# Polls before Pollsters: the corpus, then what the model does to
              it. Read the other way round the second link has no referent.
              Quieter than the forecast links. %>
          <div class="contents sm:[&>a:first-child]:ml-2">
            <%= nav_link "Polls", polls_path, quiet: true %>
            <%= nav_link "Pollsters", pollsters_path, quiet: true %>
            <%= nav_link "Methodology", methodology_path, quiet: true %>
            <%= nav_link "About", about_path, quiet: true %>
          </div>
        </nav>

        <%# The internals toggle. Off is the published forecast — independent
            polling only; on is the same model with partisan-sponsored polls
            included, adjusted and down-weighted. Every number on the site
            follows it (both variants are in the page; CSS shows one), so it
            lives in the header, not on any one chart. Hidden when JS is off:
            a control that could never do anything is worse than none, and
            the no-JS reader already has the published view. %>
        <div class="<%= app_shell? ? "col-start-2 row-start-1 flex shrink-0 items-center justify-end gap-x-1 justify-self-end xl:w-auto xl:gap-x-6 2xl:col-start-3" : "col-start-1 row-start-3 flex w-full items-center justify-end gap-x-6 max-sm:justify-between md:col-start-2 md:row-start-1 md:w-auto 2xl:col-start-3" %>" data-controller="subscribe-dialog">
          <label class="hidden min-h-11 items-center gap-2 text-slate-600 [html[data-internals]_&]:flex"
                 data-controller="internals-toggle" data-testid="internals-toggle">
            <input type="checkbox" class="peer sr-only" data-internals-toggle-target="switch"
                   data-action="internals-toggle#toggle">
            <span class="relative h-4 w-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-slate-300 transition-colors peer-checked:bg-amber-600 peer-focus-visible:outline peer-focus-visible:outline-2 peer-focus-visible:outline-offset-2 peer-focus-visible:outline-amber-600
                         after:absolute after:left-0.5 after:top-0.5 after:h-3 after:w-3 after:rounded-full after:bg-white after:transition-transform peer-checked:after:translate-x-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="leading-tight">
              <% if app_shell? %>
                <%# "Internals" is the width that fits the phone bar. The
                    accessible name stays the full term, and the sentence
                    lives in More. %>
                <span class="xl:hidden">
                  <span class="sr-only">Partisan internals</span>
                  <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-800" aria-hidden="true">Internals</span>
                </span>
                <span class="hidden text-sm font-medium text-slate-800 xl:block">Partisan internals</span>
                <span class="hidden text-xs font-normal text-slate-600 xl:block">Includes partisan-sponsored polls, adjusted</span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-800">Partisan internals</span>
                <span class="block text-xs font-normal text-slate-600">Includes partisan-sponsored polls, adjusted</span>
              <% end %>
            </span>
          </label>

          <% if app_shell? %>
            <%= link_to "Dispatches", dispatches_path,
                  class: shell_action_classes(controller_name == "dispatches"),
                  aria: { current: (controller_name == "dispatches" ? "page" : nil) },
                  data: { testid: "shell-dispatches" } %>
          <% end %>

          <%# Beside the toggle rather than in the nav: it isn't a page. As a
              ninth nav item it pushed a phone's nav onto a third line; here it
              takes the toggle row's spare width there and the header's right
              edge on a desktop. It opens the form in a dialog
              (subscribe_dialog_controller); the href is the no-JS fallback,
              the footer's copy, which every page carries. %>
          <%= link_to "Subscribe", "#subscription-form-footer",
                class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded px-2 text-sm font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600",
                data: { action: "subscribe-dialog#open" } %>

          <%# Unpadded so a click on the element itself is a backdrop click;
              the wrapper inside carries the padding. The close button comes
              after the form so showModal() focuses the email field first. %>
          <dialog data-subscribe-dialog-target="dialog" data-action="click->subscribe-dialog#closeOnBackdrop"
                  aria-labelledby="subscription-form-dialog-heading"
                  class="m-auto w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-md rounded-lg bg-white p-0 text-slate-900 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-slate-900/40">
            <div class="relative p-6">
              <%= render "shared/subscription_form", source: "dialog", layout: "dialog" %>
              <button type="button" data-action="subscribe-dialog#close" aria-label="Close"
                      class="absolute right-3 top-3 inline-flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded text-xl leading-none text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600">&times;</button>
            </div>
          </dialog>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <% if app_shell? %>
      <div data-controller="more-sheet">
        <nav class="app-tab-bar fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 border-t border-slate-200 bg-white pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)] xl:hidden" aria-label="Sections" data-testid="app-tab-bar">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-4">
            <%= link_to "Dashboard", root_path,
                  class: shell_tab_classes(shell_section == :dashboard),
                  aria: { current: (shell_section == :dashboard ? "page" : nil) },
                  data: { testid: "shell-tab-dashboard" } %>
            <%= link_to "Senate", senate_path,
                  class: shell_tab_classes(shell_section == :senate),
                  aria: { current: (shell_section == :senate ? "page" : nil) },
                  data: { testid: "shell-tab-senate" } %>
            <%= link_to "House", house_path,
                  class: shell_tab_classes(shell_section == :house),
                  aria: { current: (shell_section == :house ? "page" : nil) },
                  data: { testid: "shell-tab-house" } %>
            <%= link_to "More", "#site-directory",
                  class: shell_tab_classes(shell_section == :more),
                  aria: { current: (shell_section == :more ? "page" : nil) },
                  data: { action: "more-sheet#open", testid: "shell-more" } %>
          </div>
        </nav>

        <dialog data-more-sheet-target="dialog" data-action="click->more-sheet#closeOnBackdrop"
                aria-labelledby="more-sheet-heading"
                class="mb-0 mt-auto max-h-[min(32rem,85dvh)] w-full max-w-lg overflow-y-auto rounded-t-lg border-0 bg-white p-0 text-slate-900 shadow-xl backdrop:bg-slate-900/40">
          <div class="relative px-5 pt-4 pb-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]">
            <h2 id="more-sheet-heading" class="pr-12 font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">More</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 hidden text-sm text-slate-600 [html[data-internals]_&]:block" data-testid="shell-internals-note">
              <span class="font-medium text-slate-800">Partisan internals.</span>
              Includes partisan-sponsored polls, adjusted.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2 divide-y divide-slate-100">
              <li><%= shell_sheet_link "Polls", polls_path %></li>
              <li><%= shell_sheet_link "Pollsters", pollsters_path %></li>
              <li><%= shell_sheet_link "Methodology", methodology_path %></li>
              <li><%= shell_sheet_link "About", about_path %></li>
              <li><%= shell_sheet_link "Privacy", privacy_path %></li>
            </ul>
            <%# After the links so showModal() focuses Polls, not the close control. %>
            <button type="button" data-action="more-sheet#close" aria-label="Close"
                    class="absolute right-3 top-3 inline-flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded text-xl leading-none text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600">&times;</button>
          </div>
        </dialog>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <main id="main" class="container mx-auto px-5 <%= app_shell? ? "py-6 xl:py-10" : "py-10" %>">
      <% if flash[:notice].present? %>
        <p class="mb-6 rounded-md border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-emerald-800" role="status"><%= flash[:notice] %></p>
      <% end %>
      <% if flash[:alert].present? %>
        <p class="mb-6 rounded-md border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-red-800" role="alert"><%= flash[:alert] %></p>
      <% end %>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <footer class="border-t border-slate-200 py-10 text-sm text-slate-600 <%= app_shell? ? "mt-12 pb-10 xl:mt-24 xl:pb-[max(2.5rem,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]" : "mt-24 pb-[max(2.5rem,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]" %>">
      <div class="container mx-auto grid gap-8 px-5 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(280px,420px)]">
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <p>
            535 is an autonomous forecast newsroom — agents write from the numbers, an editor reviews.
            No secret sauce: every parameter this model uses is on the
            <%= link_to "methodology page", methodology_path, class: "font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            A project of <%= link_to "Appmakey LLC", "https://appmakey.com", class: "font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800",
                                     target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>.
            <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path, class: "ml-2 font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
          </p>
          <% if app_shell? %>
            <nav id="site-directory" aria-label="More" class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 xl:hidden">
              <%= link_to "Polls", polls_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
              <%= link_to "Pollsters", pollsters_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
              <%= link_to "Methodology", methodology_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
              <%= link_to "About", about_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
              <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path, class: "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-800" %>
            </nav>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <%= render "shared/subscription_form", source: "footer", layout: "compact" %>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
